---
import Base from "~/layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Hantavirus Cruise Tracker."
  current="privacy"
  ogType="article"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Privacy Policy", path: "/privacy/" }]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted lede">Effective date: May 8, 2026</p>

      <article class="prose">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Hantavirus Cruise Tracker (the “Site”) handles
          information when you visit. The Site is designed to be simple and privacy-respecting.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>The Site may collect the following categories of information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics data</strong>: The Site uses Google Analytics to understand aggregate
            usage (for example: which pages are visited, approximate location, device and browser
            characteristics, and referral sources). This data is used to improve the Site.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Technical logs</strong>: Like most hosting providers, the platform that serves
            the Site may process basic request metadata (such as IP address, user agent, and
            timestamps) for security, abuse prevention, and performance.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The Site does not intentionally collect sensitive personal data, and it does not require
          you to create an account.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Google Analytics may use cookies or similar technologies to measure usage. You can manage
          cookies through your browser settings and, where available, via Google’s opt-out tools.
        </p>

        <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use collected information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Understand Site performance and usage trends.</li>
          <li>Improve content quality and navigation.</li>
          <li>Protect the Site from abuse, fraud, and security threats.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information. Analytics data is processed by Google as a
          service provider. Hosting/log data may be processed by the hosting provider in order to
          deliver the Site.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          Retention periods depend on the analytics/hosting configuration. In general, we keep only
          what is reasonably necessary to understand site usage and maintain security.
        </p>

        <h2>6. International visitors</h2>
        <p>
          If you access the Site from outside the region where it is hosted, your information may
          be processed in other jurisdictions with different data protection laws.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            You can opt out of Google Analytics using browser add-ons or privacy settings (where
            available).
          </li>
          <li>You can block cookies in your browser settings.</li>
          <li>
            If you believe the Site includes inaccurate information about the outbreak, please open
            an issue with source links.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>8. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes take effect when posted on
          this page.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions, please use:
          <a href="https://github.com/judexuhs/Hantavirus-cruise">GitHub — Hantavirus-cruise</a>.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    max-width: var(--prose-max);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .prose :global(ul) {
    padding-left: var(--sp-5);
  }
  .prose :global(li) {
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-2);
  }
</style>
